  "commonsFile": "File:Arduino Uno 006.jpg",
  "editorial": {
    "history": "Unveiled in September 2010, the Uno (Italian for “one”, named for the upcoming Arduino 1.0) replaced the FTDI chip with a programmable ATmega8U2. The R3 revision introduced the “1.0 pinout” (IOREF, and SDA/SCL beside AREF) that later Arduino boards and most clones follow.",
    "today": "Still the board most tutorials, shields and classrooms assume. For new designs that need more memory or Wi-Fi, the Uno R4 keeps the layout.",
    "source": "arduino-uno-archived"
  },
